{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04DY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fc00c548e6f76cbfb1c80effff97d07ed1687f334454765a93be7874c9a2100e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe give two proofs. The first uses effectivity of descent\nfor quasi-compact, separated, <ACCENT_0001>tale morphisms relative\nto surjective integral morphisms. The second uses the material\non properties (A), (B), and (C) discussed earlier in the chapter.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2efb3f84d8fd025e35529e27cf6a74c4318f8f5c1c2bf8f72a57973dc775b67d", "unit_id": "tag:04DY:prose-0002"}
